use ../../../lib/UiComponent

export ui-component Progress:
    description:
        A progress indicator shows how far along a task is, such as an upload.
        It is either a bar that fills up, or a ring that fills round. If how
        far along the task is isn't known, it shows that something is
        happening instead.

    shapes:
        A bar runs across, or up and down if the component says so. A bar
        running across fills from the right for right-to-left languages. A
        ring fills clockwise, and the component chooses its size and how thick
        it is.

    value:
        A number between a minimum and a maximum, 0 and 100 unless the
        component says otherwise. It is kept within them. The component sets
        it as the task goes on; the user never can.

    indeterminate:
        When the component gives no value, the task's length isn't known, such
        as while connecting to a server. It then shows movement rather than a
        fill, and assistive tools are told the value isn't known. Giving a
        value later switches it back.

    valueText:
        The value can be shown as text, a percentage by default, written the
        user's local way, such as `45 %` or `45%`. The component can give
        friendlier text instead, such as "3 of 10 files". Assistive tools read
        out the same text.

    name:
        It has a name saying what is in progress, such as "Uploading
        report.pdf".

    announcing:
        Assistive tools aren't told about every change, which would be noise.
        They can find the value whenever they look at it. If the finish matters,
        the component tells them using Announcement.

    motion:
        When the user has asked their device for less motion, the movement of
        an indeterminate indicator is toned down.

    nonGoals:
        - Not something the user changes. That's a Slider
        - Not a measurement that isn't a task, such as how full a disk is.
            That's a meter
        - Not for showing which step of a longer process the user is on
